 ## Overview
-Octree Raycasting is an algorithm to find all octants in a pointer-based octree that intersect with a given ray, returning them sorted by distance (closest first) [S1, unofficial]. It uses parametric ray representation ($t$-values) to traverse the octree structure efficiently [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Octree Path Computation](897-octree-path-computation.md) by explicitly computing and sorting intersection intervals for each visited octant rather than just determining path connectivity, and from [Stackless Traversal](5202-stackless-traversal.md) by relying on a specific recursive descent logic with explicit $t$-value bounds passed down the call stack [S1, unofficial].
+Octree Raycasting is an algorithm to find all octants in a pointer-based octree that intersect with a given ray, returning them sorted by distance (closest first) [S1, unofficial]. It uses parametric ray representation ($t$-values) to traverse the octree structure efficiently [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Ray Traversal Algorithms](7918-ray-traversal-algorithms.md) by explicitly computing and sorting intersection intervals for each visited octant rather than just determining path connectivity, and differs from [Octree Path Computation](897-octree-path-computation.md) by relying on a specific recursive descent logic with explicit $t$-value bounds passed down the call stack [S1, unofficial].
 
